The function `__destroy_component_cfg` introduced in this commit (lines 1685-1688) is defined as:

c
static void __destroy_component_cfg(struct mpam_component *comp)
{
	add_to_garbage(comp->cfg);
}


It fails to check if `comp->cfg` is NULL before passing it to `add_to_garbage()`. If the component is destroyed before configuration allocation occurs, `comp->cfg` will be NULL, leading to a NULL pointer dereference when `add_to_garbage` attempts to access it.
